WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.660
It's up to you to save the human race by transforming mechanical parts into the ultimate robot warrior, MagMax.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:32.000
And welcome to NEStalgia, chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:32.900
I'm Mike.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:35.420
I'm Sean. And I'm Joe.

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:42.120
Guys, we joked about this at the end of last episode, but what does MagMax stand for?

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:45.960
Like both politically and as an abbreviation?

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:49.400
Oh, politically. What does he stand for?

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:57.940
I think MagMax stands for liberation of the people.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:59.600
Yeah. That's what I would say.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:03.460
People usually say like freedom and justice for all or something like that, you know?

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:05.220
And it's like, not really for all.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:11.280
Like he's clearly getting in the way of many other robots to clear way for everybody else.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:13.500
I think he wants to fix the potholes.

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:17.020
That's a pretty good like civic thing to stand for.

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:18.440
And that's, yeah, that's true.

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:21.040
Cause there's a, there's a reoccurring pothole in this game.

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:21.960
There's lots of potholes.

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:24.680
So it must be what he was trying to fix all along.

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:29.120
Yeah. Uh, but other than that, I have no idea like what his name is supposed to mean.

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:35.720
Um, cause I, I'm still not over the whole one letter off from Mad Max thing.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:43.600
Yeah. I think I said that as a joke last episode, but, uh, I'm starting to think like that might be like the only reason behind it.

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:44.940
Like a Mad Max sounds cool.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:47.080
Let's call it Mag Max.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:51.860
And, and there was a Mad Max trilogy by this point, you know, we, we got three of them.

00:01:51.860 --> 00:02:00.340
So it was kind of weird to, to get that close, but I suppose this is, you know, the Japanese maybe don't care for Mad Max as much as they do Rambo.

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:06.680
I suppose. Um, that's, that's a little bit presumptuous, but yeah, we'll see.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:11.260
Or maybe they did care and they knew, so they knew it would sell, uh, they would sell well as well.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:18.160
You know, it doesn't really matter how good this game is because the box art is going to set you up for disappointment.

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:19.840
Did either one of you see this box art?

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:21.760
It is fire. I did.

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:23.420
I have looking it up right now.

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:38.780
You should look it up right now because I'm telling you, if you were a kid and you went to Toys R Us and it was even 1995, you might've still bought this game thinking that you're going to be this awesome robot who takes on a three headed robotic dragon in space.

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:39.760
He's got a lightsaber too.

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:43.380
I mean, I guess I know what that might be in the game, but it does not look like that.

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:47.460
This looks like a, like an actual exact Star Wars lightsaber.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:49.160
Yeah. It's a mixture here.

00:02:49.340 --> 00:03:00.900
We have a mixture of like Star Wars, Tron, Transformers and, um, uh, Gundam, you know, like, and Godzilla for that matter, because that might as well be Mechagin Ghidorah.

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:05.420
A little bit of, uh, gravity starring, uh, Anne Hathaway.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:07.760
Oh, I see that a little bit.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:17.020
Uh, the shield blast, you know, from the, from the dragon will clearly push him out into space and the rest of the thing will be about him trying to get to the ISS.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:20.680
Yeah. I think the space here is the space from gravity.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:21.820
It's the same space.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:25.240
Yeah. Anyway, that's enough fooling around.

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:27.600
We're not going to let this, uh, this go on any longer.

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:33.000
I just thought it was worth noting that some games have really awful box arts and are good games.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:36.860
Other games just have like middle of the road box art and the games like whatever.

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:41.020
And then you have games that have pretty sick box art, but turn out to be shmups.

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:46.620
Which is what MagMax is.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:50.900
MagMax is a shmup, uh, fought with a transforming robot.

00:03:51.220 --> 00:04:03.360
Uh, the player can transform, uh, from a ship into a robot, increasing, uh, their power as you build this robot with its head and its legs and a cannon for its stomach.

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:07.700
Uh, and you can fight more than 30 different enemies according to the box.

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:10.140
That's pretty cool too. Yeah.

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:13.840
Um, so I think like these are the selling points of the game, right?

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:17.800
But get a robot or have a ship and turn it into a robot.

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:19.840
That sounds really cool as a concept, right guys?

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:21.200
Yeah, I think so.

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:31.540
Um, what this game sort of, uh, made me realize about myself is that I needed, because shmups are so, are so different from pretty much anything else.

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:38.400
I needed a different kind of way to score and like, I needed a rubric for shmups.

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:42.740
And I've, I've got like a few categories if, if you will indulge me.

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:44.520
Please don't. Yeah.

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:48.520
So one is like, you know, is the gameplay good?

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:50.220
Does it have any interesting elements?

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:52.560
Uh, sure. That's, that's the one.

00:04:52.800 --> 00:05:05.280
And the other one is like, does it have anything ridiculous that means nothing in terms of how good the game is, but like, at least it's something like visually different?

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:07.260
And that's the other.

00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:11.660
And the third is, does it, does it need to exist?

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:13.180
And the answer to that is always no.

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:19.800
No, but with, with this game at like the fact that you aren't like, just, you're not a ship.

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:26.400
You are a, an anthropomorphized robot that actually walks across the screen.

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:28.460
That was different enough for me.

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:34.300
And I, my, my bar is so low now that I was just happy to see something different like that.

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:35.380
I don't know about you guys.

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:37.320
I mean, I agree.

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:46.840
The, the, the fact that there's this, this anthropomorphic ship and the fact that you like collect, instead of just collecting power-ups, you're collecting like pieces of your ship as you go through.

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:48.180
Yeah. Building yourself. Mostly legs.

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:50.040
As you go through. Yeah.

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:53.680
Yeah. Yeah. The legs, I will, I will say though, the legs are the silliest part.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:57.240
Like you look really silly once you have the legs.

00:05:57.440 --> 00:06:07.500
Well, what's silly is that, what's silly is that there, there's all of these parts of your, of your robot scattered throughout the land and you pick them up as you go.

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:12.860
And if you don't need the legs, like if you already have them, it's just like, oh, I'm just gonna leave those legs over here.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:13.920
Like you can't do anything.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:15.560
I just like, just leave those legs over there.

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:18.200
I might need them when I like loop through this game again.

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:21.720
Yeah. But the idea of a mech is, is pretty cool.

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:26.000
Right, Joe? Like, like the idea that you would become this all powerful robot.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:38.180
Like we're always talking about power-ups being an important, smart, important part of shmups, but to actually see your ship grow into a robot is a lot cooler than just like, I got a new cannon that shoots lightning.

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:49.520
Exactly. Yeah. And it, you know, seeing it, you're like building loosely what's on the front cover, you know, there is that lightning cannon, which I assume is supposed to be a lightsaber.

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:51.080
Yeah. Yeah. Yeah.

00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:53.900
Um, so I, I thought it was pretty cool.

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:59.800
Although I would have liked the power-ups to do like most of the power-ups just give you an extra gun.

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:01.100
