00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:03.300
And then like one or two give you something unique.

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:09.320
Would have been cool if they all had something like that changed, you know, like that wasn't just the same gun.

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:13.780
Like the feet just shoot lasers, but like, it doesn't look like there's anywhere that lasers would come out.

00:07:13.880 --> 00:07:15.100
They're just feet. They come at the toe.

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:17.620
So I thought that was like, yeah, it's just come out of the toe.

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:18.960
It looks like it is wearing shoes.

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:20.740
So maybe they're laser shoes.

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:21.680
I think they are.

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:29.320
Yeah. Yeah. I'm realizing now that all my complaints about this game are about the feet, but, but, but, but no, it just looks goofy.

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:31.020
But I, you know, I did think it was cool.

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:36.240
Yeah. I think, uh, Quentin Tarantino would love this game then if that's, if that's all the complaints you have.

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:43.180
Yeah. You know, shouldn't there have been more mech loadouts though, than just like these same pieces floating across.

00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:59.820
Like, wouldn't it have been cool if instead of legs, you got like a submarine base or something like, or instead of the generic head that you have, there's like this awesome head that does something, you know, like instead of shooting a projectile, it, uh, it can take two hits or something.

00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:01.920
I just think of like a Mega Man style thing.

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:08.220
That's a cool, I didn't think of it that way as in like you mix and match your pieces and build kind of your, whatever robot you end up with.

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:16.980
Yeah. That's a cool, because, because I did have a little bit of a, a wish at least that like, that you could continue to collect more things.

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:19.460
Cause it does seem like you can get the full robot pretty quickly.

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:22.580
I thought like, well, there's a lot of time in later levels.

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:34.800
I feel like maybe what if you could just keep adding on things, but I think I like your idea a little better where it's like, you can build a robot of like these five pieces, but there's a bunch of different combinations of different, you know, different heads, different legs.

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:44.880
Yeah. That is something I never, I didn't actually think about, but that would make this game much more, uh, it's much more satisfying to play.

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:47.660
If you could sort of tailor it to your own play style.

00:08:47.820 --> 00:09:01.560
Cause like the, the, um, the novelty of walking around instead of flying around wears off pretty quickly, especially because yeah, you get, you get these parts very quickly.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:14.720
Um, and when I was like reading the manual before this, I thought like having a complete robot was going to be like, not that there's like an end game in these kinds of games, but I thought that would be much more difficult to come across.

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:19.820
And it's, it's pretty pedestrian, um, once you finally get it.

